(3825342, 538978, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 2/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 1/2<br/> <br/>I really like the colors in the photo. The greens and purples are amazing. I like how dark the background is, but feel that, although it supports the subject well, it doesn''t really make it stand out to me and stun me when I look at it. I think the DOF is too shallow, and would like to see the entire flower in focus. The stray green leaf? coming through the photo really doesn''t do much except lead me out of the photo.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2Contrast/Color: 2/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 1/2 I really like the colors in the photo. The greens and purples are amazing. I like how dark the background is, but feel that, although it supports the subject well, it doesn''t really make it stand out to me and stun me when I look at it. I think the DOF is too shallow, and would like to see the entire flower in focus. The stray green leaf? coming through the photo really doesn''t do much except lead me out of the photo.', '2007-06-23 19:06:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(3825348, 539628, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 2/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 2/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 2/2<br/> <br/>I really like this image. I only gave it a 1 for the challenge because I feel that the negative space, although it is nice and complementary on the left, is completely barren on the right, and therefore does not "wow" me. The title leaves me thinking where the rest of the life of the raindrop is in the negative space. Other than that, I love everything about this image. I think the crisp detail is stunning, and the very limited DOF really makes the water and drop stand out also. The lighting is perfect, illuminating just this branch while the others appear to be not only out of focus, but also in the shadows. Nice work.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2Contrast/Color: 2/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 2/2My Subjective Affinity: 2/2 I really like this image. I only gave it a 1 for the challenge because I feel that the negative space, although it is nice and complementary on the left, is completely barren on the right, and therefore does not "wow" me. The title leaves me thinking where the rest of the life of the raindrop is in the negative space. Other than that, I love everything about this image. I think the crisp detail is stunning, and the very limited DOF really makes the water and drop stand out also. The lighting is perfect, illuminating just this branch while the others appear to be not only out of focus, but also in the shadows. Nice work.', '2007-06-23 19:08:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(3825355, 539942, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 0/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 1/2<br/>Composition: 1/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 0/2<br/> <br/>Although there is negative space in this photo by definition, it does nothing to support the eye. It is just dark nothingness. I think the phot would benefit with the inclusion of something so support your main subject, and a bit more light. The whole thing just looks extremely underexposed.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 0/2Contrast/Color: 1/2Composition: 1/2Photo Quality: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 0/2 Although there is negative space in this photo by definition, it does nothing to support the eye. It is just dark nothingness. I think the phot would benefit with the inclusion of something so support your main subject, and a bit more light. The whole thing just looks extremely underexposed.', '2007-06-23 19:13:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(3825358, 540023, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Contrast/Color: 2/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 2/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 1/2<br/> <br/>The only thing that I think could improve this shot would be to use an ND grad filter on the sky so that there is some detail in the foreground. Nice work.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Contrast/Color: 2/2Composition: 2/2Photo Quality: 2/2My Subjective Affinity: 1/2 The only thing that I think could improve this shot would be to use an ND grad filter on the sky so that there is some detail in the foreground. Nice work.', '2007-06-23 19:14:48.000000', NULL, 1),
