(3840523, 539142, 63398, '<td valign="top">A truly awesome photograph! You should take pleasure in this for years after this challenge is forgotten. A beautiflu, timeless shot! Congratulations!</td>', 'A truly awesome photograph! You should take pleasure in this for years after this challenge is forgotten. A beautiflu, timeless shot! Congratulations!', '2007-06-27 07:08:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3840529, 538962, 28710, '<td valign="top">What a fascinating way to present negative space! i really, really like this one. So many things to like about this one.<br/> <br/>The rocks in black are strong and overbearing and perfect. A little closer inspection reveals a tiny bit of detail splashed around the edges which subliminally carries into the shadow area and looks good.<br/> <br/>The repeating theme and rhythym coming through the rest of the image is a major defining feature of what is really great about this image for me. It''s all about light, water and rocks. The way it all flows into radial lines from the lower right to top left, creating bands of color, luminosity and texture while moving down the left edge further reinforces the minimalistic subject which is in just the right color (although the nitpick is that the red it just a hair too strong there and I mean just a hair - likely more a result of resizing than anything).<br/> <br/>Definitely a great pick for this challenge.<br/> <br/>If I could make some suggestions for post-challenge, maybe bring out the spray as it breaks on the coast towards the right just a teeny bit, go to the blues channel and very slightly play with desaturating and darkening to push the contrast just a bit and get rid of the high saturation areas on the left edge.<br/> <br/>In-challenge this would have been a 10 from me and my pick for blue.</td>', 'What a fascinating way to present negative space! i really, really like this one. So many things to like about this one. The rocks in black are strong and overbearing and perfect. A little closer inspection reveals a tiny bit of detail splashed around the edges which subliminally carries into the shadow area and looks good. The repeating theme and rhythym coming through the rest of the image is a major defining feature of what is really great about this image for me. It''s all about light, water and rocks. The way it all flows into radial lines from the lower right to top left, creating bands of color, luminosity and texture while moving down the left edge further reinforces the minimalistic subject which is in just the right color (although the nitpick is that the red it just a hair too strong there and I mean just a hair - likely more a result of resizing than anything). Definitely a great pick for this challenge. If I could make some suggestions for post-challenge, maybe bring out the spray as it breaks on the coast towards the right just a teeny bit, go to the blues channel and very slightly play with desaturating and darkening to push the contrast just a bit and get rid of the high saturation areas on the left edge. In-challenge this would have been a 10 from me and my pick for blue.', '2007-06-27 07:10:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3840531, 539142, 9821, '<td valign="top">awesome, awesome, awesome</td>', 'awesome, awesome, awesome', '2007-06-27 07:11:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3840548, 538454, 28710, '<td valign="top">another fantastic result of using negative space to enhance the primary subject. The first glance at the thumbnail made me feel that by pushing the suit down to the black point, you had made the image uncomfortably arranged and I didn''t like it.<br/> <br/>Click on that thumbnail and this thing unfolds on the desktop. <br/> <br/>Stunningly managed gradients and textures. Beautifully controlled whites. Those alone define the image as intentional, and thus begins the eye''s journey into why.<br/> <br/>the missing suit jacket becomes an implication. Something you expect to see but don''t.<br/> <br/>What a powerful counterpoint for the tragedy of his eye.<br/> <br/>Totally brilliant and excellent in every way. I don''t usually just look at an image just to look at it as long as I did for this one. I just sat and stared. I hope that says enough.</td>', 'another fantastic result of using negative space to enhance the primary subject. The first glance at the thumbnail made me feel that by pushing the suit down to the black point, you had made the image uncomfortably arranged and I didn''t like it. Click on that thumbnail and this thing unfolds on the desktop.  Stunningly managed gradients and textures. Beautifully controlled whites. Those alone define the image as intentional, and thus begins the eye''s journey into why. the missing suit jacket becomes an implication. Something you expect to see but don''t. What a powerful counterpoint for the tragedy of his eye. Totally brilliant and excellent in every way. I don''t usually just look at an image just to look at it as long as I did for this one. I just sat and stared. I hope that says enough.', '2007-06-27 07:18:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3840567, 539561, 23394, '<td valign="top">told ya so ;-)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by debi:</b></div><hr/><i>any title suggestions?<table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skip:</b></div><hr/><i>"Mostly Sunny with a Chance of Flowers"</i></td></tr></table></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>congrats on you 6+ finish!!</td>', 'told ya so ;-) Originally posted by debi:any title suggestions?Originally posted by skip:"Mostly Sunny with a Chance of Flowers"  congrats on you 6+ finish!!', '2007-06-27 07:32:21.000000', NULL, 0),
