(3842032, 535088, 51793, '<td valign="top">ouch that sucks... but rules are rules. Doesn''t mean that it''s still not a good picture. I gave it a 10 for what it''s worth to ya.</td>', 'ouch that sucks... but rules are rules. Doesn''t mean that it''s still not a good picture. I gave it a 10 for what it''s worth to ya.', '2007-06-27 14:21:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842035, 535345, 50695, '<td valign="top">just to expand on my cryptic comment, there is of course negative space in this photo. The trouble is that the squared-off shape of your subject doesn''t make that negative space interesting. Usually, negative space is emphasized when it has its own shape. The classic example is two faces looking at each other. The space between the two faces looks like a vase. See the wikipedia entry for negative space.</td>', 'just to expand on my cryptic comment, there is of course negative space in this photo. The trouble is that the squared-off shape of your subject doesn''t make that negative space interesting. Usually, negative space is emphasized when it has its own shape. The classic example is two faces looking at each other. The space between the two faces looks like a vase. See the wikipedia entry for negative space.', '2007-06-27 14:22:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842051, 539552, 58728, '<td valign="top">Wow.  Very creative.  I really like this.</td>', 'Wow.  Very creative.  I really like this.', '2007-06-27 14:25:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842062, 539552, 78114, '<td valign="top">ohhhhhhhhhh, now i get it! that''s pretty cool! very creative!</td>', 'ohhhhhhhhhh, now i get it! that''s pretty cool! very creative!', '2007-06-27 14:29:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842075, 538454, 80296, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot.  I am new here at DPC and want more information about so many photographs. It would be great to read more about the technical aspects of this shot.  Where was the zoom set - f-stop and shutter settings - existing light conditions and auxiliary lighting.  Post processing steps.<br/>Thanks for submitting this entry</td>', 'I like this a lot.  I am new here at DPC and want more information about so many photographs. It would be great to read more about the technical aspects of this shot.  Where was the zoom set - f-stop and shutter settings - existing light conditions and auxiliary lighting.  Post processing steps.Thanks for submitting this entry', '2007-06-27 14:33:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842099, 539609, 42013, '<td valign="top">How cool is this?! It''s like his broken down car spilled all his wares onto the ground and they are just waiting for their owner. <br/> <br/>To me the negative space is created by the relative uniformity of all of the hats, interrupted only by the guy and his car.</td>', 'How cool is this?! It''s like his broken down car spilled all his wares onto the ground and they are just waiting for their owner.  To me the negative space is created by the relative uniformity of all of the hats, interrupted only by the guy and his car.', '2007-06-27 14:41:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842176, 535345, 40580, '<td valign="top">Thanks Posthumous for comming back and commenting.  Ya, I should''ve ditched the square crop and made the thimble smaller to emphasize the negative space.  I have some better ideas for Negative Space IV.<br/> <br/>Sorry hipychik, but I can''t flag your comment as helpful.  Maybe it is helpful in the fact that the title is too obscure, but that''s what I was kinda going for.  It''s a reference to Peter Pan.<br/></td>', 'Thanks Posthumous for comming back and commenting.  Ya, I should''ve ditched the square crop and made the thimble smaller to emphasize the negative space.  I have some better ideas for Negative Space IV. Sorry hipychik, but I can''t flag your comment as helpful.  Maybe it is helpful in the fact that the title is too obscure, but that''s what I was kinda going for.  It''s a reference to Peter Pan.', '2007-06-27 15:01:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842220, 539238, 61961, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gipomontesanto:</b></div><hr/><i> Thank you for ur comments and ur votes. I think this photo perfectly matches with the description: "...use the surrounding space of your subject to create the wow of the photograph..."</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Gipo, I did not see it this way when I voted, but you are right: according to the challenge description, your photo fits.  Anyway, as I commented earlier I like your photo and I did not score it too low. :-)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by gipomontesanto: Thank you for ur comments and ur votes. I think this photo perfectly matches with the description: "...use the surrounding space of your subject to create the wow of the photograph..." Gipo, I did not see it this way when I voted, but you are right: according to the challenge description, your photo fits.  Anyway, as I commented earlier I like your photo and I did not score it too low. :-)', '2007-06-27 15:15:47.000000', NULL, 0),
